--- body ---

## Context

Child of tracker `0648`. `R15-uninstall-removes-declared-state` can pass when
install materialized no state and uninstall removed nothing. Its survivor scan
counts regular files, so an empty owned directory can remain after uninstall
without falsifying "none of that state may remain".

## Exit criteria

- [ ] prove target-created derived state materialized before uninstall or report
      `not-run`
- [ ] state which declared roots or owned entries must disappear versus become
      empty, based on the target's real uninstall surface
- [ ] detect surviving directories, symlinks and other applicable owned entries
- [ ] retain event-then-state ordering and never perform cleanup for the target
- [ ] red controls cover no-op install/uninstall and empty-directory residue
- [ ] `make check` passes
